{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 46.6% a year from $6.91 billion in FY2017 to $215.9 billion in FY2026 [F1][F10][F211]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The window is a step change, not a smooth compound: revenue was flat at 0.2% growth in FY2023, then rose 125.9% in FY2024, 114.2% in FY2025 and 65.5% in FY2026 [D284][D338][D393][D448]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2024 step came from Data Center revenue up 217% on Hopper GPU shipments for LLM training and inference [P22][P23]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2026 growth was driven by data center compute and networking platforms, with Blackwell the majority of Data Center revenue [P10]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Data Center was 89.7% of FY2026 revenue and contributed 60.2pp of the 65.5% growth [D620][D622][D448]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Within it, Data Center computing grew 59% on Blackwell demand and networking grew 142% on NVLink for GB200 and GB300 systems [P8]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating income grew 60.1% against revenue growth of 65.5%, an incremental operating margin of 57.3% [D449][D448][D475]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 24.8pp slower than revenue in FY2026, at 40.7% [D476][D468]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Diluted EPS rose 66.7% against net income growth of 64.7%, with the diluted share count down 1.2% [D452][D450][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating margin of 60.4% in FY2026 sits well above the 32.8% window median but below the 62.4% FY2025 high and far above the 15.7% FY2023 low [F50][D813][D812][D811]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Gross margin fell 3.9pp to 71.1% as cost of revenue grew 91.4% against revenue growth of 65.5% [D462][F30][D465][D448]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 operating margin slipped 2.0pp, with cost of revenue a 3.9pp drag partly offset by R&D and SG&A at 1.3pp and 0.6pp [D463][D477][D478][D479]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2026 net margin of 55.6% sat 4.8pp below the 60.4% operating margin, despite $11.1 billion of other income [F70][F50][D861][X120]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $102.7 billion was 0.86x net income, below the 0.97x window median and the 0.86x window low [F100][F60][D435][D851][D850]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow of $96.7 billion was a 44.8% margin, against a 44.4% window median and a 46.6% FY2025 high [F110][D432][D822][D821]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex of $6.04 billion was 2.8% of revenue and 2.13x D&A, up from 1.74x in FY2025 [F105][D431][D437][D382]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Investing outflows of $52.2 billion rose on higher equity investment purchases and a non-exclusive license agreement with Groq [F120][P1]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Cash and investments of $43.2 billion against total debt of $8.47 billion left net cash of $34.7 billion, or 26.6% of revenue in FY2025 [D384][D440][D386][D387]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2026 net-cash figure is not comparable: short-term investments were not reported in FY2026 though reported in FY2025, so the pack omits them and the values built on them [R3]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Return on average equity of 101.5% ranks at the 100th percentile of six semis peers against a 20.3% median [D447][D848][D849]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $40.1 billion plus dividends of $974 million were 42.5% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count fell 1.2% [X150][X160][D444][D470]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Short-term investments were not reported in FY2026 though reported at $34.6 billion in FY2025, so net cash and cash and investments for FY2026 omit them [R3][X188]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "This is a data gap rather than a deterioration, but it makes the FY2026 net-cash comparison and peer rank unusable until the line is filed."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Graphics was 44.1% of revenue and fell 25.0% in FY2023, a one-period decline [D753][D754][R1]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The segment has since recovered to $22.5 billion of FY2026 revenue, so the flag reads as cyclical rather than structural [S125]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether gross margin holds above the 71.1% FY2026 level or falls further as cost of revenue grows faster than revenue, in the FY2027 10-K [F30][D465][D448]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether operating cash flow to net income recovers above the 0.97x window median from 0.86x, in the FY2027 10-K [D435][D851]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether Data Center revenue growth stays above the 68.2% FY2026 rate or decelerates, in the FY2027 10-K [D621]."}
  ]}
]}
